BASE=ROOT/'shard/root_substances'; OUT=BASE/'kg26'; CAP=BASE/'captures'; NOW=datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat()
INDICES=list(range(161,185))+[186,187]
def sha(p):return hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()
def digest(a):return hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(a,sort_keys=True,separators=(',',':'),ensure_ascii=False,allow_nan=False).encode()).hexdigest()
def save(p,a):p.write_text(json.dumps(a,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n')
R={
161:('broad_parent_relation_only','The nine admitted rows in media 1191, 1279, 1600 and 1793 consistently specify demineralized water, including one sterile addition in 1600. Original DSMZ recipes retain demineralized water (Aqua dem. in 1279). The current Distilled_Water owner already marks this label REJECTED_LABEL: a common H2O molecular parent does not establish the same water treatment or purity preparation. This case is a preparation-qualified solvent; neither distilled nor tap water is asserted as its exact identity.','Keep the rejected alias boundary and distinct demineralized preparation. CHEBI:15377 can supply a molecular parent only; source-scoped operational water identity would require a treatment/purity record, rather than reversing the rejected alias.','A supported demineralized-water owner with a source-defined preparation/purity scope is required before exact local resolution; no ion-removal method or quantitative purity specification is stated.'),
162:('existing_identity_or_alias','Both complete source recipes, DSMZ 1003 and 1146, add 30 mg Na-tungstate x 2 H2O to one litre of trace-mineral solution adjusted to pH 3. Current ChEBI:63939 explicitly denotes sodium tungstate dihydrate, formula 2H2O.2Na.O4W and CAS 10213-10-2, matching the existing Na2wo4_X_2_H2o owner and its hydrate-form alias. This supports the exact dry reagent identity at these two recipe positions; it does not identify the resulting trace stock with that reagent. The complete published row remains withheld because its other channel includes a 0.1% preparation, Na2WO2 errors and anhydrous-parent names.','No source-label addition or owner identity change is necessary for the scoped hydrate correspondence. Do not release the entire withheld SSSOM payload: its unrelated alias, preparation and evidence obligations remain independently reviewable.',None),
163:('stock_product_mixture_context','The admitted full J451 recipe adds 30 ml of 84 g/L NaHCO3 solution, autoclaved under CO2, after the basal recipe is sterilized and cooled under N2/CO2. This supports a concentration-defined prepared bicarbonate stock and the existing local stock record as a source-label candidate, not neat CHEBI:32139 identity. The live JCM451 response is Nothing found and supplies no formulation evidence; the admitted 2026-11-05 MediaDive body supplies the actual recipe claim. Current owner aliases include the bare fragment (5% w/v solution), which denotes 50 g/L if applied to this bicarbonate stock and therefore cannot name an 84 g/L stock, and the non-name (after autoclaving).','The exact prepared stock remains source scoped. The only proposed owner edit rejects the two demonstrably non-identifying fragments while preserving their original text and provenance; it does not approve the remaining complete owner or release a withheld mapping.',None),
164:('existing_identity_or_alias','The exact metatraits graph node names 2-deoxythymidine-5\'-4-nitrophenyl Phosphate and explicitly points to its MIM record; its raw_source_label is blank and is preserved. The existing MIM owner uses the identical kgmicrobe.compound local registry identifier, and the admitted consumed row already supports that registry reference with an empty other field. This is exact local registry continuity only. No CAS, structure or external ontology identity is inferred from spelling; stereochemical/structural detail and biological utilization claims are outside this decision.','The current owner and admitted registry mapping already express the source-local identity. No additional alias, external chemical mapping or observational edge rewrite is warranted.',None),
165:('stock_product_mixture_context','All 98 embedded material dispositions retain H2+CO2 as a reported joint substrate condition: 93 Bergey rows and five Literature rows. Every row has identity_approved false and identity_status unresolved, with its original subject, citation, source-column and raw-record hash preserved. This plus-sign expression records a combined gas condition, without any global ratio; it cannot be split into independent H2-only and CO2-only utilization claims. The lexical search has no resolving owner for this exact source token. Contextual H2_CO2 history is not an assertion that its record owns all 98 observations.','Retain all 98 joint-condition assertions and their original citations. A single ingredient identity, common gas ratio or redirection of the graph object is unsupported; no owner is invented to satisfy native review tooling.','A source-scoped interpretation per original taxon observation would be needed for any gas ratio or chemical identity redirect; the existing joint-condition disposition is already adequate for the literal observations.'),
166:('stock_product_mixture_context','DSMZ1433 specifies 5 g Sigmacell alpha Type 50 (Sigma S5504). The current official S5504 page identifies Sigmacell Cellulose, Type 50, 50 micrometres, CAS 9004-34-6, and separately lists alpha-cellulose C6429 as another product. The catalog code therefore supports this specific cellulose product, while the recipe word alpha is retained as source wording rather than used to assert a polymorph, alpha-cellulose grade or different catalog identity. The existing UNMAPPED_0520 is the corresponding source-label placeholder; bulk cellulose equivalence would lose the Type50 physical product detail.','Preserve the specific S5504 product scope and unresolved owner status until product-qualified modeling is integrated. No generic cellulose exact identity or transfer to the separate alpha-cellulose product is proposed.','For product promotion, bind a vendor-qualified S5504/Type50 record and its physical form; establish whether historical alpha wording was an old product designation before treating it as an identity synonym.'),
167:('supplied_form_correction','Both DSMZ1493 and1685 specify 0.440 g Na2SeO4 x 10 H2O in the shared one-litre trace solution, after dissolving nitrilotriacetic acid and adjusting pH. The supplied form is explicitly sodium selenate decahydrate. Current Na2seo4.yaml denotes CHEBI:77775, whose official structure and formula 2Na.O4Se are anhydrous; it already rejects the decahydrate alias. The hydrate must remain distinct. Its formula is source supported, but assigning the anhydrous identifier to it would erase ten waters.','Retain the rejected-label boundary. No edit to the anhydrous owner is needed, and no new form-specific identifier is minted without a registry/ontology check and a distinct-record proposal.','Verify an authoritative decahydrate-specific identifier or CAS and any existing distinct-form owner before promoting this source material; anhydrous CHEBI:77775 can at most be the related parent.'),
168:('existing_identity_or_alias','The metatraits graph node has name Proteose, blank raw label and xref MIM:Proteose. The maintained owner and consumed supported row refer to the same kgmicrobe.compound:proteose local registry entity. This establishes registry continuity for the literal source node only. Proteose is not proven identical to a commercial proteose-peptone digest, any specified protein substrate or a molecular species. The single count is a graph incident edge, not medium frequency.','Keep the existing local registry correspondence. No product composition, protein origin, new alias or external ontology grounding is inferred.',None),
169:('malformed_or_nonchemical_token','The admitted MediaDive row and original DSMZ863 PDF both literally print Na2Se2O3, 0.100 g in the trace-element stock. The current Na2seo3 owner/ChEBI:48843 represents disodium selenite, formula 2Na.O3Se; its RAW_TEXT Na2Se2O3 came from an earlier merge, not an inspected source correction. The additional selenium atom in the source formula cannot be silently removed. The recipe may contain a typographic defect, but neither the original PDF nor current source provides a correction to Na2SeO3.','Preserve the source token and the existing downstream mapping hold. No alias approval or exact redirect to disodium selenite is supported; an old merge rationale does not repair the primary source.','An authoritative correction for the DSMZ863 trace-component formula, or original formulation evidence specifying the actual reagent, is needed to resolve the malformed selenium formula.'),
170:('stock_product_mixture_context','The full JCM978 recipe uses 5 ml Mineral solution (see Medium No. 976, including its unclosed parenthesis. The referenced source is JCM976, not DSMZ976. Its mineral stock is EDTA 3.7 g, FeSO4·7H2O 1.1 g, MnCl2·4H2O 98.4 mg, ZnSO4·7H2O 28.8 mg, CoCl2·6H2O 23.8 mg, CuCl2·2H2O 17.2 mg, Na2MoO4·2H2O 24.2 mg and H3BO3 31.0 mg in 1 L distilled water, adjusted to pH6 with KOH. The existing local stock record is lexical continuity but lacks components and incorrectly names DSMZ976 in its history. The raw punctuation defect does not make the preparation scientifically uninterpretable.','The complete recipe-specific formulation is recovered and should drive a typed stock decomposition; the existing owner is not approved wholesale because its source attribution and component evidence need correction. No cross-collection recipe substitution is allowed.','Integrate a source-qualified JCM976 stock with component assertion provenance and a typed JCM978 use reference; correct the erroneous DSMZ976 attribution without rewriting history as though it had been right.'),
171:('stock_product_mixture_context','JCM722 specifies 3 g Hy-Case Amino (Sigma) in CYS medium. Sigma/Millipore C0501 explicitly calls Hy-Case Amino a bovine-milk casein acid hydrolysate, powder, predominantly free amino acids with some peptides, and reports 25-40% sodium chloride. This supports the branded acid digest product and contradicts equivalence to intact casein, an enzymatic casein digest, or a single amino acid. The recipe has no lot or catalog number, so C0501 is current supplier product corroboration rather than proof of the exact historical lot.','Retain the UNMAPPED_0404 product scope and source spelling. Product-qualified promotion can use the recovered acid-digest identity; a generic hydrolysate exact merge or fixed component percentages is not justified.','A product-qualified owner and explicit historical/current supplier applicability decision are needed before promotion; ingredient composition must retain ranges and undefined mixture scope.'),
172:('stock_product_mixture_context','JCM969 uses 10 g EBIOS dried yeast tablets and footnotes Asahi Food & Healthcare, Tokyo. The current official Asahi EBIOS tablet page confirms dried yeast tablets and lists lactose hydrate, calcium hydrogen phosphate, anhydrous silica and hardened oil as excipients. It does not establish the historical recipe lot formulation, but it demonstrates that the branded tablet is not interchangeable with pure yeast extract or the EBIOS P2G extract discussed in the owner’s old research. The source material here is the tablet preparation.','Preserve UNMAPPED_0380 as a source/product placeholder; do not adopt the old yeast-extract interpretation. The current supplier details are supporting product context and are not backdated quantitative composition claims.','Define a tablet-specific owner and establish historical formulation applicability before component-level curation; do not use yeast-extract or P2G equivalence.'),
173:('existing_identity_or_alias','The gtdb-metatraits graph node names Beta-D-galacto-pyranosyl-D-arabinose and explicitly xrefs the same-named MIM record. The current owner and supported consumed row use the identical local registry identifier. Blank raw_source_label remains blank. Registry continuity is supported, while the name does not state the galactosyl linkage position on arabinose, so no specific external disaccharide structure or linkage is invented.','The local registry reference already preserves the exact graph source name. No external ontology term, CAS or complete structural equivalence is added.',None),
174:('stock_product_mixture_context','The one MediaDive ID572 occurs in three distinct supplied contexts. DSMZ559 uses 2 ml of 5% w/v Na-thiosulfate stock, prepared under N2 and filter sterilized. DSMZ1840 adds 10 ml/L of a 2 M aqueous stock before inoculation. DSMZ1903 uses 10 g dry Na-thiosulfate in TCBS agar, dissolved by heating without autoclaving; no hydrate is stated. The shared ID does not authorize one global exact supplied-form mapping to the anhydrous Na2s2o3 owner. The admitted559 g_l=1667 and mmol_l=10543.3 are derived quantities incompatible with the stated stock addition and are not identity evidence.','Keep each recipe preparation distinct and retain the existing mapping hold. Sodium thiosulfate is the common solute interpretation, but neither stock is the neat reagent, and the dry occurrence does not establish a hydrate.','Resolution must be by recipe occurrence/qualifier, with separate 5% and2M stock contexts and a dry-form decision for1903; correct the derived559 quantity upstream without replacing raw amount or unit.'),
175:('unresolved','All104 admitted media rows across103 media and29 overlapping solution rows specify Na2B4O7 x10H2O; the exact frozen source rows and full recipe bodies are preserved. One row in DSMZ770 is explicitly a0.1%w/v stock added at1.8ml, also confirmed by the original PDF, and cannot be treated as neat hydrate. The other source contexts retain the decahydrate reagent formula. The maintained owner and official CHEBI:131366 name decahydrate, yet its current formula10H2O.H4B4O9.2Na and structure expand to Na2B4H24O19, two H2O more than source Na2B4O7·10H2O (Na2B4H20O17). A label/CAS match therefore cannot approve the current exact assertion or imported chemical properties.','Preserve source hydrate specificity and the separate770 stock context. Do not approve the whole mapping payload or silently normalize the ontology formula while it disagrees with the source formula.','Resolve CHEBI:131366 formula/structure hydration accounting with authoritative ontology or structural evidence, verify the complete owner chemical properties, and keep the7700.1%stock occurrence separate before releasing exact mapping.'),
176:('existing_identity_or_alias','The metatraits node is the separate source case for Beta-D-galacto-pyranosyl-D-arabinose, with blank raw label and its own one-edge count. It explicitly xrefs the current MIM owner using the identical kgmicrobe.compound registry ID; the supported consumed registry row has an empty other field. Local registry continuity is supported independently of the gtdb-metatraits case. The unstated glycosidic linkage position prevents claiming a specific external disaccharide structure.','Preserve this source case separately and retain the existing registry correspondence. No duplicate observation merge, new structural identifier or alias expansion is proposed.',None),
177:('existing_identity_or_alias','The gtdb-metatraits graph node separately names 2-deoxythymidine-5\'-4-nitrophenyl Phosphate and xrefs its MIM owner with the identical local kgmicrobe.compound ID. Its three incident edges and blank raw label are retained separately from the metatraits eight-edge case. The consumed supported registry row establishes local reference continuity only; spelling does not supply a verified CAS, full structure or external chemical identity.','Keep the existing registry mapping with no new chemical grounding, alias expansion or merger of source-specific counts.',None),
178:('existing_identity_or_alias','DSMZ843 explicitly uses 0.05 g ß-NAD in one litre of Co-factors solution, adjusted to pH7 and filter sterilized. The current owner preserves the sharp-s source spelling, while the official CHEBI:15846 record lists β-NAD/beta-NAD and NAD among its synonyms with CAS53-84-9. This supports the scoped source label as oxidized beta nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide, not NADH or alpha-NAD. The recipe does not establish the protonation state of dissolved material at pH7; this is the reagent-name correspondence, not a solution-speciation assertion. The prior consumed hold concerns property data-source attribution and independent mapping review rather than a demonstrated different reagent.','The source alias and matching owner already exist. Keep unresolved chemical-properties provenance and any whole-payload release outside this scoped positive label/identity decision; no duplicate record or speculative salt correction is needed.',None),
179:('unresolved','The metatraits graph source says rubradirin and has the process synonym produces: rubradirin, with no B suffix, structure or xref establishing the congener. The current owner maps exactly to CHEBI:223718, which the official ontology explicitly names Rubradirin B with formula C40H33N3O15. That specificity is not supplied by the source. The process phrase has already been marked non-resolving in the current owner; its removal is not the remaining identity problem.','Retain the source node and existing mapping hold. Do not infer Rubradirin B from unsuffixed rubradirin or treat production wording as a compound alias.','Source-specific evidence identifying which rubradirin congener was reported, followed by a congener-specific owner/ontology correction, is required before exact resolution.'),
180:('stock_product_mixture_context','The admitted589 main recipe uses1000ml water(distilled or tapwater), an operational alternative rather than a physical mixture of two waters. The original DSMZ589 PDF instead prints Distilled water1000ml and does not authorize the tapwater alternative. This is a concrete MediaDive-versus-original-source scope discrepancy. The current UNMAPPED_0575 preserves the phrase but its undefined-mixture classification does not resolve the disjunction.','Retain the exact admitted source label and conflict. Do not redirect it globally to Distilled_Water or treat tapwater and distilledwater as exact aliases; no fictitious two-water mixture is proposed.','Resolve the origin and intended validity of the MediaDive589 tapwater alternative; then model a recipe choice or correct the source occurrence, rather than minting a single mixture identity.'),
181:('unresolved','The gtdb-metatraits rubradirin graph case has its own one-edge count and literal process synonym produces: rubradirin, but no congener qualifier. Official CHEBI:223718 is specifically Rubradirin B. The same current MIM owner’s exact mapping therefore remains unsupported for this independent source case, even though the process phrase was already excluded from resolving aliases.','Preserve the independent source case and mapping hold; neither the metatraits counterpart nor the common string proves B-congener identity.','Obtain congener-identifying evidence for this gtdb-metatraits source assertion and a matching owner before publishing a Rubradirin B exact relation.'),
182:('stock_product_mixture_context','DSMZ727 uses5g Lab Lemco powder(Oxoid); admitted CCAP C23 andC26 use1g OxoidL29 perlitre, andC27 uses that ingredient in its EG submedium mixed1:1withJM. Current CCAP originals confirm the Lab-Lemco quantities and nesting. The official Oxoid LP0029 specification identifies a refined powder meat-extract product with bounded analytical properties, not a molecular chemical or an arbitrary beef extract. The earlier ThermoL0029B capture is an error wrapper and supplies no scientific support.','Preserve the existing UNMAPPED_0419 product identity and exact supplier context. A product-qualified owner may use the LP0029/L29 evidence without collapsing all meat extracts or inventing fixed component stoichiometry.','Integrate a vendor-qualified Lab-Lemco owner with supplier specification provenance and explicit L29/LP0029 catalog continuity; do not promote solely through a generic meat-extract ontology exact match.'),
183:('stock_product_mixture_context','DSMZ581 specifies5g Cornsteep powder in Glycerol Cornsteep Agar, alongside separate yeast extract, beef extract and casein peptone. Both admitted source and original PDF establish the dry corn-steep product class but give no vendor, drying process or lot composition. The current UNMAPPED_0366 is the matching powder placeholder. A liquid corn-steep liquor record or a carbohydrate/protein molecule would erase the stated physical mixture form.','Retain a distinct corn-steep powder product class with undefined biological mixture composition. No exact merge with liquor or inferred molecular components is warranted.','Product-class curation needs a supported powder-specific parent/identifier and process scope; vendor-specific composition must await an identified product specification.'),
184:('broad_parent_relation_only','The admitted row and original DSMZ969 specify Na-tetrathionate/Natetrathionate0.10g perlitre in Sulfobacillus medium atpH1.8. Sodium counterion is explicit; no hydration or catalog grade is given. The UNMAPPED_0463 owner preserves this exact source label. Potassium tetrathionate, thiosulfate, tetrathionate ion alone and a specified sodium hydrate are not exact substitutions for this source reagent.','Retain the sodium tetrathionate source placeholder and common tetrathionate relationship only. No form-specific ontology or registry identifier is assigned from an unspecified hydrate.','Verify the sodium salt’s supplied hydrate/form or a supported form-unspecified sodium-tetrathionate identity before exact promotion; do not borrow the potassium-salt identifier.'),
186:('stock_product_mixture_context','DSMZ863 fully defines Sodium carbonate solution: dissolve106g Na2CO3 in1litre degassedH2O, then autoclave in sealed serum bottles underCO2; add24ml to the basal medium. This is source-specific formulation evidence, not an unspecified carbonate stock. The current Sodium_Carbonate_Solution owner is typed as a stock but uses neat-compound CHEBI:29377 and carries anhydrous reagent, buffer and malformed aliases. Official CHEBI:29377 describes the dry carbonate formula CO3.2Na, not this prepared solution. The admitted g_l59.7638 is not used as a stock formulation.','Retain the recovered106g/L preparation as source-scoped stock context. Reusing or editing this owner requires resolving its mixed aliases and stock-versus-neat identity first; merely changing one mapping predicate would leave inconsistent identity.','Prepare a qualified stock record and reconcile the current owner’s neat-reagent aliases/identifier against all its source contexts, with component evidence and CO2/sterilization qualifiers.'),
187:('malformed_or_nonchemical_token','The admitted973 row and original DSMZ973 PDF both literally state Na2Se3 x5H2O0.50mg. The existing owner and official CHEBI:131361 denote Na2SeO3·5H2O, disodium selenite pentahydrate, with formula5H2O.2Na.O3Se. Adding the missing oxygen and replacing Se3 by SeO3 is a plausible correction, but the original source itself does not verify it. The old RAW_TEXT alias therefore cannot independently establish the reagent’s identity.','Retain the exact raw formula and downstream hold. No source repair, exact alias approval or redirection to the pentahydrate owner is justified by lexical plausibility alone.','Obtain an authoritative correction or original formulation identifying the DSMZ973 selenium reagent before accepting Na2SeO3·5H2O as the intended supplied form.')}
